@startuml F20-grant-lifecycle
title F20 — Cycle de vie d'un crédit fidélité (activation différée + validité 60 j)

[*] --> issued : issueGrant (commande OK)\ncode FG-<MOT>-<NNNN>\nactivatesAt = orderDate + maxDeliveryDays(eta) + 1j\nexpiresAt = activatesAt + 60j

state "issued\n(emis, non encore utilisable)" as issued
state "active\n(fenetre ouverte, redeemable)" as active
state "redeemed\n(consomme, usage unique)" as redeemed
state "expired\n(validite depassee)" as expired

' --- validateGrant(now) : etats observables par la cliente ---
issued --> issued : validateGrant, now < activatesAt\n=> reason = not_yet_active (activatesAt fourni)
issued --> active : now >= activatesAt\n(borne incluse : now === activatesAt => valide)\n(INV-ACTIVATION)

active --> active : validateGrant, activatesAt <= now <= expiresAt\n=> valid (valueCents)
active --> redeemed : redeemGrant(code, orderId)\n(usage unique)
active --> expired : now > expiresAt\n(borne incluse : now === expiresAt => valide)\n(INV-VALIDITY)
issued --> expired : jamais active puis now > expiresAt

redeemed --> redeemed : validateGrant => reason = already_redeemed\n(prioritaire sur expired / not_yet_active)
expired --> expired : validateGrant => reason = expired

note right of issued
  IDEMPOTENCE a l'emission :
  - même sourceOrderId => MÊME grant (INV-IDEMP-ORDER)
  - même phoneE164 actif => grant existant renvoye (INV-IDEMP-PHONE, anti-farming)
  Un seul code actif par telephone.
end note

note bottom of active
  Conséquence UI : code dictable, message
  « utilisable à partir du JJ/MM ». validateGrant
  est NON mutante (previsualisation). reason inconnu => not_found.
end note
@enduml
